# Line endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows and deployed to Linux. Git's default
# on Windows checks files out with CRLF, which is harmless for Python but fatal
# for anything the Linux kernel has to execute directly: a shell script whose
# shebang line ends `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` fails with
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# which names neither the file nor the real problem. systemd units and cloud-init
# YAML are parsed leniently enough that CRLF usually survives, but not reliably,
# so they are pinned too.
#
# These rules apply on checkout regardless of the developer's core.autocrlf.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
